  "worked_solution": "The given set contains the roots $x\\in R$ of some quadratic polynomial $p(x).$\n\nSince the polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=1$ and ${x}_{2}=\\sqrt{2},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=3,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2}) \\\\  & =3(x-1)(x-\\sqrt{2}) \\\\  & =3({x}^{2}-(\\sqrt{2}+1)x+\\sqrt{2}) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}-3(\\sqrt{2}+1)x+3\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can express the given set as follows:\n\n$$\n{1,\\sqrt{2}}={x\\in R\\,:\\,3{x}^{2}-3(\\sqrt{2}+1)x+3\\sqrt{2}=0}\n$$",
